    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "I0\n7\n10\n9\n8\nPRATT \u0026 WHITNEY AIRCRAFT\nTWIN WACO\nHORSEPOWER CURRECTION FOR\nCARBURETOR AIR TEMPERATURE VARIATION\nNote: ADD correction if carburetor air scoop\ntemperature is BELOW standard.\nSUBTRACT correction if carburetor air\nscoop temperature is ABOVE standard.\nSTANDARD ALTITUDE TEMPERATURES\n1000 3METERS4\n60\n15\n10\n40\nSTAND\nTEMP\n-100\n0\n-10\nS.L.\n5 1000 10 FEET 15\n- 20\n20\nHORSE POWER CORRECTION\nCARB. AIR TEMP. DIFF.\nHORSEPOWER\nRANGE\nOF\n°C\n9\n5\n18\n27\n36\n45\n10\n15\n20\n25\n300-350\n350-400\n400-450\n450-500\n500-550\n550-600\n600-650\n650-700\n700-750\n750-800\n800-850\n850\n9\nO\n91\n950\n•11\n1000-1050\n1050-111\nOO\n1100-1150\n1150-1200\n6\n8\n11\n14\n3\n7\n1\n1\n1\nO\n1\n3\n16\n15\n18\n2\n1\n7\n20\n2:\n3\n54\n30\n17\n20\n22\n25\n2\n7\n25\n6\n6\n7\n7\n7\n8\n8\n1\n1\n1\n27\n33\n3!\n1\n1\n1\n1\n9\n1\n1\n1\n1\n2\n3\n4\n5\n6\n7\n8\n8\n1\n9\n20\n2\n1\n5\n6\n8\n1\n9\n20\n20\n22\n24\n21\n5\n2\n7\n29\n3\n32\n2!\n9\n3\n33\n35\n2:\n3\n24\n25\n27\n21\n8\n9\n31\n8\n41\n6\n41\n8\nS\n4,\n2\n44\n3\n6\nC\n5\nBREMO HUNDREDS\nP\u0026WA\n1945ml\nPC-10",
      "PRATT \u0026 WHITNEY AIRCRAF\nTWIN WASP 2SDU\n20\nAUTOMATIC RICH - LOW\nARISATIO\n1100\nALTITUDE IN THOUSANDS OF FEET\n500\n*\u0026 WA\n1945\nPC-10\n9\n8\n7\n6\n5\nPRATT\nAND\nWHITNEY AIRCRAFT\nCRUISING POWER CALCULATOR\nINSTRUCTIONS\nUse the curve below to determine the most\neconomical RPM for the desired brake horse-\npower.\nHold calculator so that pressure of fingers\non slide through opening will keep the slide\nfirmly against indexing edge at left of case.\nSet observed altitude on diagonal top edge\nhorizontally opposite horsepower desired.\nAt\nintersection of diagonal top edge and desired\nRPM, read necessary manifold pressure.\nCorrect horsepower for carburetor air scoop\ntemperature (not mixture temperature) accord-\ning to tables on reverse side.\n1000\n900\nSMER\n11.\n800\nQ.\nI\n700\n600\n500\n15\n16\n17\n18\n19\n20\n2l\n22\nRPM HUNDREDS\n23\n24\n25\n26\n27"
